## Models
######Entities - any object, person, concept, or event about which data is stored.*
***

### AdminUsers (Models/AdminUsers.cs)
Represents an admin/guest account. Inherits from `IdentityUser<Guid>`, so username,
email, and password hashing are handled by ASP.NET Identity — not custom fields.
Maps to the `Users` table (renamed from `AdminUsers` via `.ToTable()` in
ApplicationDbContext).

- Adds: `CreatedAt`, `LastLogin`, and a 1—1 nav property to `Logs` (audit trail).
- Role (Admin/Guest) is NOT a field on this class — it's handled separately via
  Identity's `Roles`/`UserRoles` tables, seeded in `OnModelCreating` and checked with
  `[Authorize(Roles = "Admin")]`.
- Default admin seeded in `Program.cs` (admin@example.com / Admin123! — change before
  deploying, it's currently in plain text).

### AskAQuestionEmails (Models/AskAQuestionEmails.cs)
A contact-form submission — just `Email` and `isActive` (likely a subscribe/unsubscribe
flag rather than a full message form).

**Status: modeled but unused.** Natural fit for wiring up the currently-empty
Contact Us page.

### Classes (Models/Classes.cs)
A language class/course being offered (e.g. "Beginner Chinese"). Bilingual title +
description, `StartDate`, `CreatedAt`/`UpdatedAt`. Has two nav collections:
`Schedules` (→ `ClassSchedule`) and `Signups` (→ `ClassSignups`).

**Status:** admin Create/Overview exist. Public page is an empty shell — `Index()`
returns a view with no data pulled from this table yet.

### ClassSchedule (Models/ClassSchedule.cs)
A recurring time slot for a `Classes` entry — `DayOfWeek`, `StartTime`, `EndTime`
(both `TimeOnly`). FK `ClassId` → `Classes`. Lets one class have multiple weekly
sessions (e.g. Tue/Thu 6–7pm).

**Status: modeled but unused** — no controller reads/writes this yet.

### ClassSignups (Models/ClassSignups.cs)
A registration form submission for a class — `Name`, `Age`, `Email`, `Phone`,
`ClassType`, `HSKLevel` (Chinese proficiency test level), `CreatedAt`. FK `ClassId` →
`Classes`. This is what a visitor fills in on the public Classes page to sign up.

**Status: modeled but unused** — no controller reads/writes this yet. This is the
natural companion piece to building out the public Classes page.

### ErrorViewModel (Models/ErrorViewModel.cs)
Framework boilerplate, not app data — carries a `RequestId` for the default error page
(`Views/Shared/Error.cshtml`). No DB table, not part of the schema. Leave as-is.

### Event (Models/Event.cs)
A one-off event (talk, festival, screening, etc.). Bilingual title/description,
`Photographer`/`Author`/`Translator` credit fields, `Status` ("Draft" by default —
implies a draft/published workflow), `Tickets` (string flag, default "NoTickets"),
`DateOfEvent`, `Deadline` (signup cutoff), timestamps. No FKs — Images attach to it via
the polymorphic `Image.ItemType="Event"` pattern instead of a real relation.

**Status: your most complete feature.** Public Index + full admin
Create/Edit/Overview/Delete + image upload/delete.

### Image (Models/Image.cs)
A single uploaded image — `FilePath`, bilingual `AltText`, `SortOrder`, `CreatedAt`.
Polymorphic association via `ItemType` (string, e.g. "Event", "PageSection") +
`ItemId` (int) instead of a real foreign key, so one table serves images for multiple
entity types. Trade-off: flexible, but EF can't validate or eager-load the link — a
dangling `ItemId` pointing at a deleted row is possible. Fine for now; consider real
per-entity FKs if you have time before the deadline.

### Logs (Models/Logs.cs)
Audit trail entry. One row per tracked action (create/edit/delete etc.) — `Action`,
`EntityType`, `EntityId`, `Description`, `CreatedAt`. Optional FK `UserId` → `AdminUser`
(nullable, so a log entry can exist without a user attached, e.g. system events).
1—1 with `AdminUser` as configured in `OnModelCreating`.

**Status: modeled but unused** — nothing in the controllers currently writes to this
table. Not required to demo a working site; add later as polish if time allows.

### NavigationList (Models/NavigationList.cs)
A navigation menu entry — `Type`, bilingual `Label`, `Position`, `IsVisible`. Optional
FK `PageId` → `Pages` (nullable, so a nav item doesn't strictly need to point at a
CMS page — could link elsewhere, e.g. to `/Events`).

**Status: modeled but unused.** Your site nav is presumably hardcoded in
`Views/Shared/_Layout.cshtml` right now instead of driven by this table.

### News (Models/News.cs)
Same shape as `Event` but for news posts — bilingual title/description, `Status`,
optional `Tickets`, `ValidUntil` instead of a deadline, timestamps. Also no FK; also
uses the polymorphic Image pattern if it has images.

**Status:** public Index + admin Create/Overview exist. **No admin Edit action yet** —
smallest gap to close, same pattern as Events' Edit.

### Pages (Models/Page.cs)
A dynamic content page in the (unfinished) CMS system — bilingual menu label + title,
`Slugs` (URL path), `IsVisible`, `SortOrder`, timestamps. Nav collections: `Sections`
(→ `PageSections`) and `NavigationItems` (→ `NavigationList`).

**Status: stub.** `Areas/Admin/Controllers/PagesController` only has an empty
`Index()`. This is the biggest unfinished piece — likely what would drive the Team
page and any other static content, but not required for a basic working demo.

### PageSections (Models/PageSections.cs)
A block of content within a `Pages` entry — `SectionType` (e.g. "text", "gallery" —
exact types not yet defined anywhere), bilingual description, `SortOrder`. FK `PageId`
→ `Pages`. Lets one page be built from multiple ordered content blocks.

**Status: modeled but unused**, part of the same unfinished CMS system as `Pages`.

### Settings (Models/Settings.cs)
Singleton-style table (expected to hold one row) for homepage content — contact
address/phone, a cover image, and three bilingual image+paragraph pairs for the
homepage sections.

**Status: modeled but unused** — `Views/Home/Index.cshtml` is presumably hardcoded
right now instead of reading from this table. Self-contained, no dependencies on
other unfinished features — good candidate to build next.

